  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Virginia recorded $97B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state had 348,913 awards with an average award size of $278K. Obligations fell 19.5% year over year. The FY21 to FY26 series shows obligations of $77.9B in FY21, $89.4B in FY22, $106B in FY23, $110B in FY24, $121B in FY25, and $97B in FY26. The Department of Defense obligated $34.8B and the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $32.9B in FY2026 to date. OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. received $19.9B and TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP received $9.5B in FY2026 to date. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers accounted for $29.4B and Computer Systems Design Services accounted for $10.3B in FY2026 to date. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies drive Virginia's federal contracting?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $34.8B in FY2026 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $32.9B, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $7.1B and the General Services Administration with $5.3B. Lower-ranked buyers include the Department of Health and Human Services with $3.6B and the Department of Justice with $2.5B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors and industries receive the most obligations?",
        "body": "OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. received $19.9B and TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP received $9.5B in FY2026 to date. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers accounted for $29.4B and Computer Systems Design Services accounted for $10.3B. Other large vendors include ATLANTIC DIVING SUPPLY, INC. with $3.6B and LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION with $3.1B."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Virginia?",
      "a": "Virginia received $97B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 348,913 awards with an average award size of $278K, and obligations were down 19.5% year over year. FY21 to FY26 figures were $77.9B, $89.4B, $106B, $110B, $121B, and $97B respectively."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Virginia?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense and the Department of Veterans Affairs award the most contracts in Virginia. The Department of Defense obligated $34.8B and the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $32.9B in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security and the General Services Administration followed with $7.1B and $5.3B respectively."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are the largest federal contractors in Virginia?",
